-- CA_0153_la_trustee_area_boards_batch4b1.sql
-- LA-County TRUSTEE-AREA unified school boards, batch 4b-1 of the roster refresh (CA_0143, CA_0145,
-- CA_0147, CA_0148): Glendale, Inglewood, Long Beach, Pasadena.
-- Operator decision 2026-09-22 for these districts: "rosters + trustee areas". Same pattern as the
-- parallel trustee-area session's CA_0144 / CA_0146 (whose generator this file is built with): one
-- X0002 polygon + SCHOOL sub-district per area, dissolved from the LA County Registrar-Recorder precinct
-- layer (Political_Boundaries/MapServer/34, DST_USD/DIV_USD, read 2026-09-22; USD codes 15 Glendale,
-- 36 Inglewood, 16 Long Beach, 30 Pasadena); the generic 'Board Member' offices move off the
-- whole-district row; stale holders closed (how_ended 'unknown', end date not researched --
-- operator decision 2026-09-22); current members seated from each district's own board page.
-- NO RACES are seeded here (none of these four has a CA_0142 race; see NOT DONE).
--
-- AREA-NUMBER DECODE -- anchored per district (DIV_USD N = the district's own area N):
--   Glendale (lettered A-E): the district's adopted 2021 trustee-area map (GUSD redistricting web map,
--     ArcGIS item d71d8cac..., layer "Glendale USD 2021 Adopted Trustee Election Areas", DISTRICT A-E)
--     overlaps DIV 1..5 by 99.2 / 94.3 / 99.3 / 99.9 / 99.9 % -> A=1 .. E=5. The NetFile committees
--     "Telly Tse for Glendale School Board Area A 2024" / "Neda Farid ... Area E 2024" agree.
--   Inglewood: all 8 schools the district lists per trustee area (Kelso -> TA1; Centinela, La Tijera
--     -> TA2; Bennett-Kew, Woodworth-Monroe -> TA3; Inglewood High, Oak Street, Beulah Payne -> TA5)
--     fall in DIV of the same number.
--   Pasadena: the City of Pasadena open-data layer "Pasadena Unified School Districts"
--     (services2.arcgis.com/zNjnZafDYCAJAbN0/.../Pasadena_Unified_School_Districts) DISTRICT 1..7
--     overlaps DIV 1..7 by >= 99.8 % each.
--   COVERAGE GATE: Long Beach's TIGER polygon (980.8 km2) includes open ocean around the port and
--     Catalina; its five areas total ~379 km2 of land, so for Long Beach the gate checks that the areas lie
--     INSIDE the TIGER polygon (>= 97 %) instead of matching its area. The other three match within 0.5 %.
--   Long Beach: District 1 = "California Heights, Bixby Knolls and North Long Beach" (LAist 2026 guide)
--     -- all three geocode into DIV 1; District 5 = "the airport and the areas north and east of it"
--     (Long Beach Post) -- the airport geocodes into DIV 5.
--
-- BATCH-SPECIFIC:
--   * SIX stale holders are VERIFIED current members and are KEPT (row + open 1459 term untouched,
--     CA_0145 §C / 1546 precedent), each office pinned to the member's area: Erik Miller (LB D2), Juan
--     Benitez (LB D3), Diana Craighead (LB D5), Kim Kenne (Pasadena D1), Michelle Bailey (Pasadena D3),
--     Yarma Velázquez Vargas (Pasadena D7). Their stored party is cleared.
--   * Two stale seats are pinned to the stale holder's REAL area so the handover date is exact, with
--     how_ended 'term_expired' (§5b): Shant Sahakian (Glendale D) and Pat Cahalan (Pasadena D4).
--   * Glendale and Long Beach elect with the statewide PRIMARY. Glendale seats winners in July (the
--     2026 cohort took the oath 2026-07-14); its March 2024 winners' start month is not sourced
--     (precision year). Long Beach seats winners in December (2022 odd districts sworn in Dec 2022), so
--     its June 2026 winners (López D1, Craighead D5, Benitez D3) begin their NEW terms in Dec 2026 --
--     the current terms are the 2022 ones.
--   * Pasadena has 6 seats for 7 districts: one seat is added (clone), per the operator decision.
--   * Nine members reuse confirmed LA County NetFile rows (campaign-finance links): Telly Tse, Neda
--     Farid, Margaret Evans, Ernesto Castillo, Doug Otto, Jennifer Hall Lee, Scott Harden, Tina
--     Fredericks -- three with an unfinished imported name completed (§4a).
--
-- 🔴 NOT DONE HERE, AND OWED: Inglewood (TA 1-3) and Pasadena (Districts 1, 3, 5, 7) have seats on the
-- Nov 3 2026 ballot, but no 2026 race exists for either -- their candidates file with the city clerk,
-- so they are absent from the RR/CC candidate list CA_0142 was built from. Stale holders keep party
-- 'Nonpartisan' and is_active true.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT: every insert NOT EXISTS-guarded; office moves guarded on the whole-district row;
-- stale-term closing only touches open terms not held by the named member.
BEGIN;

CREATE TEMP TABLE _seat (parent_geo text, geo_id text, label text, ta text, ord int, full_name text, first_name text,
                         last_name text, url text, existing_pid uuid, term_start date, prec text, how text, src text,
                         pin_office uuid, vacant_since date, aw text, pid uuid) ON COMMIT DROP;
